<title>ITALY: CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO RESULTS AND STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-TIRRENO-ADRIATICO RESULTS AND STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>PESCASSEROLI, Italy 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>leading results in</p>
<p>the second 131-km stage of the Tirreno-Adriatico cycle race from</p>
<p>Venafro to Pescasseroli on Friday (Italian unless stated):</p>
<p>1. Davide Casarotto three hours 33 minutes eight seconds</p>
<p>2. Roberto Petito same time</p>
<p>3. Beat Zberg (Switzerland) two seconds behind</p>
<p>4. Francesco Frattini</p>
<p>5. Vassily Davidenko (Russia)</p>
<p>6. Massimiliano Gentili</p>
<p>7. Gianluca Pianegonda</p>
<p>8. Luc Leblanc (France) all same time as Zberg</p>
<p>9. Massimo Donati 15 seconds</p>
<p>10.Rolf Aldag (Germany) two minutes 40 seconds</p>
<p>Leading standings:</p>
<p>1. Petito eight hours 25 minutes 39 seconds</p>
<p>2. Pianegonda two seconds</p>
<p>3. Zberg eight seconds</p>
<p>4. Casarotto 15 seconds</p>
<p>5. Gentili 17 seconds</p>
<p>6. Frattini same time</p>
<p>7. Davidenko 19 seconds</p>
<p>8. Leblanc 20 seconds</p>
<p>9. Donati 46 seconds</p>
<p>10.Rolf Sorensen (Denmark) two minutes 46 seconds</p>
</text>
